# Dopemux Beta-Readiness — Sequenced Backlog

Run metadata: HEAD `755bf3846`, 2026-05-29. Severities/effort/disposition transcribed from the audit synthesis; every item's evidence lives in `00-MASTER-REPORT.md` (path:line).

---

## Internal-Beta Blockers (dogfood gate)

| id | title | severity | domain | effort | depends_on | fix_summary |
|----|-------|----------|--------|--------|------------|-------------|
| BETA-CLI-01 | `dopemux decisions` group ships only energy+patterns; review/list/show/update-outcome/query subcommands absent | HIGH | CLI | M | — | The decisions surface is the user-facing read/write path over ConPort decision records. With only energy/patterns subgroups, a dogfooder cannot list, show, review, or update-outcome decisions from the CLI — a core ADHD-workflow flow. Implement the missing subcommands (review/list/show/update-outcome/query) against the ConPort client, mirroring the energy/patterns group structure. |
| BETA-MCP-01 | `.mcp.json` conport/dope-memory SSE URLs use `${CONPORT_MCP_PORT}`/`${DOPE_MEMORY_PORT}` with no `:-` default — empty-port URL if launcher not run first | HIGH | MCP | S | — | If Claude Code is launched without first running the instance-overlay launcher that exports these vars, both SSE URLs resolve to `http://localhost:/mcp` (empty port) and ConPort + dope-memory MCP fail to connect — breaking the primary memory/knowledge flow for you and close users. Add `:-3005` / `:-3020` defaults matching the compose defaults (or guarantee the launcher always exports them). Kept on BOTH gates conservatively; downgrade to public-only ONLY if the dogfood launcher is proven to always export the port vars (currently NOT proven — see open_unknowns). |
| BETA-SURF-01 | Orchestrator `/dx:` command surface regressed off main by PR #720 — `.claude/commands/dx/` now contains only `implement.md` | MED | Tooling | M | — | A stale Jules/Gemini palette PR (#720) reverted the CLAUDE-SURFACE orchestrator command surface (the `/dx:` slash commands + orchestrator config.yaml + protocol). The runtime hooks from #722 are still present, but the operator-facing dx command surface is gone, degrading the dogfooding workflow. Restore the surface by cherry-picking the deleted files from `origin/task-orchestrator-claude-surface`. Scope is the `.claude` tooling surface (author/dogfood workflow), not end-user product flow — hence MED. |
| BETA-HOOK-01 | Stop hook blocks session exit once per stop when a workflow is active and no checkpoint/completion-token emitted (friction, not hard lockup) | LOW | Hooks | S | — | Only bites a user who tries to end the session mid dopemux-workflow with no emitted checkpoint. The block fires once, then `stop_hook_active` lets the next exit through, so it is recoverable confusion rather than a lockup. For polish, add an explicit `dopemux workflow abandon` escape or a time/iteration-based auto-release so the first block isn't surprising. Low priority for internal beta. |

