## Post-Beta (non-gating)

| id | title | severity | domain | action | effort | depends_on | fix_summary |
|----|-------|----------|--------|--------|--------|------------|-------------|
| BETA-CLEAN-01 | Remove dead/stub services: `services/router` (only `__init__`) and `services/dope-query` (no server) | OBS | Cleanup | remove | S | — | These two service directories have no runnable server and no compose service. They add navigation noise and imply capability that does not exist. Delete them (or move to an explicit `/experiments` area). NOTE: dope-memory is NOT in this set — it is an active service (compose builds it from services/working-memory-assistant/Dockerfile.dope-memory and ships mcp_stdio_adapter.py); the inherited 'dope-memory duplicates working-memory-assistant' claim is refuted. |
| BETA-MCP-04 | Document shared-Postgres single-role/dev-credential posture; confirm migration 007 ordering for advanced graph features | OBS | MCP | document | S | — | Data-plane isolation for ConPort holds on a fresh install (workspace_id is a partition key; active_context is per (workspace_id, instance_id) via _ensure_schema-added column). Two doc items remain: (1) all services share one Postgres role/DB with dev-default credentials — fine for single-tenant local, must be hardened/documented before any shared deployment; (2) document which migrations beyond instance_id are auto-applied vs require manual run, since start_with_info.sh has no migration step. |

