## Sequencing Waves — Ordered Roadmap

### Wave 0 — restore/unblock

**Items:** `BETA-SURF-01`

Restore the orchestrator `/dx:` command surface stripped by PR #720 before doing further dogfood work, so the workflow surface the rest of the backlog assumes is actually present. Recover from `origin/task-orchestrator-claude-surface`. No code dependencies; do first because it is pure restore and unblocks operator workflows.

### Wave 1 — internal-beta gate (dogfood)

**Items:** `BETA-CLI-01`, `BETA-MCP-01`

Close the two confirmed internal-dogfood blockers: the missing decisions subcommands (RV-3, core CLI flow) and the empty-port `.mcp.json` risk (MCP-6, connection of core memory MCPs). BETA-MCP-01 also benefits the public gate. Independent of each other; can run in parallel.

### Wave 2 — public-beta gate

**Items:** `BETA-INSTALL-01`, `BETA-MCP-02`, `BETA-MCP-03`

The external-user delta: clean-machine install (hardcoded task-orchestrator path), cold-start races (service_healthy), and multi-instance Redis safety. BETA-INSTALL-01 first (highest external impact), then the two compose/runtime items. No hard dependencies among them but all should land before any external clone is attempted.

### Wave 3 — polish/cleanup

**Items:** `BETA-HOOK-01`, `BETA-CLEAN-01`, `BETA-MCP-04`

Non-gating: Stop-hook UX escape valve, deletion of dead router/dope-query stubs, and documentation of shared-Postgres credential posture + migration ordering. Safe to defer until after both beta gates are green.

